]]></ns6:summary><ns6:author><ns6:name>José Parra Moyano</ns6:name><ns6:bio><![CDATA[Jos&#233; Parra Moyano is a professor of digital strategy at IMD. He studies how companies can use and implement digital technology to create real value and applies the insights of his research in his work with organizations across all industries, translating evidence from field data and experiments to advise boards and executive teams.]]></ns6:bio><ns6:uri>https://hbr.org/resources/images/article_assets/2023/10/110-jose-parra-moyano.jpg</ns6:uri></ns6:author><ns6:author><ns6:name>Karl Schmedders</ns6:name><ns6:bio>Karl Schmedders is a professor of finance at IMD in Lausanne, Switzerland, and a visiting professor of executive education at the Kellogg School of Management in Evanston, Illinois. He holds a PhD in operations research from Stanford University. His work uses the tools of finance and economics to analyze how artificial intelligence and climate change affect companies.</ns6:bio></ns6:author><ns6:author><ns6:name>Olivier Laplace</ns6:name><ns6:bio>Olivier Laplace is a partner at venture capital firm Vi Partners. He has more than two decades of experience as a tech entrepreneur and intrapreneur, software developer, investment banker, and venture capital investor.</ns6:bio></ns6:author><ns6:author><ns6:name>Benjamin Torben-Nielsen</ns6:name><ns6:bio>Benjamin Torben-Nielsen is an executive at Roche. He holds a PhD in Artificial Intelligence and Neuroscience.</ns6:bio></ns6:author><ns6:feature-image-uri sizes="(min-width: 48em) 55.7291667vw, 97.3924381vw" srcset="https://hbr.org/resources/images/article_assets/2026/10/Oct26_16_AnaMoreno-383x215.jpg 383w, https://hbr.org/resources/images/article_assets/2026/10/Oct26_16_AnaMoreno-300x169.jpg 300w, https://hbr.org/resources/images/article_assets/2026/10/Oct26_16_AnaMoreno-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://hbr.org/resources/images/article_assets/2026/10/Oct26_16_AnaMoreno-768x432.jpg 768w, https://hbr.org/resources/images/article_assets/